WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.725
A filesystem organises persistent data and metadata.

00:00:02.725 --> 00:00:08.176
A file name identifies a directory entry; a path explains how to reach it.

00:00:08.176 --> 00:00:13.627
Absolute paths start from a root, while relative paths depend on a current directory.

00:00:13.627 --> 00:00:17.520
File extensions are naming conventions, not proof of content type.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:26.020
If the working directory is the project root, the file is inside notes and its relative path is notes/chapter1.txt.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:29.178
Opening only chapter1.txt looks in the current directory.

00:00:29.178 --> 00:00:33.125
The failure should be diagnosed before creating a duplicate file.

00:00:34.125 --> 00:00:37.229
A relative path is interpreted from what location?

00:00:37.229 --> 00:00:39.945
Its meaning depends on the working directory.
